        "kind": "figure",
        "label": "Figure 2.5",
        "caption": "Knowledge Graph enhanced Natural Language Inference - From [56]: To tackle NLI tasks, KNGLI encodes the premise and the hypothesis into knowledge graphs. Using an attention-based model to derive a semantic representation of the textual information in the two input sentences and a GNN to obtain a knowledge-relation encoding from their structured version, this architecture obtains a deeper understanding of the interaction between the premise and the hypothesis. After pooling, the two hidden representations are merged to produce a probability distribution over the set of labels.",
